#: fa006045842b4a5d884ff9c16212f00b
msgid "How-to guides"
msgstr ""

#: c6fd9544ec244bddb8ebb16e965ddd49
msgid "How-to guides are **directions** that guide the reader through a problem or towards a result. How-to guides are **goal-oriented**."
msgstr ""

#: 972e062fb76d4ed798453256c4d23bae
msgid "A how-to guide helps the user get something done, correctly and safely; it guides the user's *action*."
msgstr ""

#: 5ef2a8978d5b4c0f91e3b7412d908eee
msgid "It's concerned with *work* - navigating from one side to the other of a real-world problem-field."
msgstr ""

#: 0f40e908589e4e1eadd76ed7e6485bc8
msgid "How-to guides - task oriented, practical steps, that serve our work"
msgstr ""

#: 3265fd4cc386478197b56d4ccf80f0ef
msgid "Examples could be: *how to calibrate the radar array*; *how to use fixtures in pytest*; *how to configure reconnection back-off policies*. On the other hand, *how to build a web application* is not - that's not addressing a specific goal or problem, it's a vastly open-ended sphere of skill."
msgstr ""

#: 3f3b2c95e1224b6c838334152339782c
msgid "How-to guides matter not just because users need to be able to accomplish things: the list of how-to guides in your documentation helps frame the picture of what your product can actually *do*. A rich list of how-to guides is an encouraging suggestion of a product's capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: 085f163fa55b4ae594c3904567009939
msgid "Well-written how-to guides that address the right questions are likely to be the most-read sections of your documentation."
msgstr ""

#: 66fa7fc9788e4ca083974eb9db3e27a7
msgid "How-to guides addressed to problems"
msgstr ""

#: a849880af8bf42cc9a086c8cb8768dc2
msgid "**How-to guides must be written from the perspective of the user, not of the machinery.** A how-to guide represents something that someone needs to get done. It's defined in other words by the needs of a user. Every how-to guide should answer to a human project, in other words. It should show what the human needs to do, with the tools at hand, to obtain the result they need."
msgstr ""

#: 81e095c1a0224a8a97cf060cd2ef0387
msgid "This is in strong contrast to common pattern for how-to guides that often prevails, in which how-to guides are defined by operations that can be performed with a tool or system. The problem with this latter pattern is that it offers little value to the user; it is not addressed to any need the user has. Instead, it's focused on the tool, on taking the machinery through its motions."
msgstr ""

#: ec10173cf15549d2baadc2ac7240e779
msgid "This is fundamentally a distinction of *meaningfulness*. Meaning is given by purpose and need. There is no purpose or need in the functionality of a machine. It is merely a series of causes and effects, inputs and outputs."
msgstr ""

#: 9f84cc1f39c34556ba6d3350f885ec03
msgid "Consider:"
msgstr ""

#: 04b3254efccb42c6a67cc67380ac6b85
msgid "\"To shut off the flow of water, turn the tap clockwise.\""
msgstr ""

#: 875a2edb0efe4f74acb9b704f0f196c9
msgid "\"To deploy the desired database configuration, select the appropriate options and press **Deploy**.\""
msgstr ""

#: 93d394aba54249db96d56c32d29d3d40
msgid "We really do not need to be informed that we turn on a device using the power switch, but it is shocking how often how-to guides in software documentation are written at this level."
msgstr ""

#: 306a1874cfdd4db39009cc32b4687639
msgid "The examples above *look* like examples of guidance, but they are not."
msgstr ""

#: 2723cb82a4b549eea34d1885ff6f09c9
msgid "They represent mostly useless information that anyone with basic competence - anyone who is working in this domain - should be expected to know. Between them, standardised interfaces and generally-expected knowledge should make it quite clear what effect most actions will have."
msgstr ""

#: 949a992f99f04ff2a60385b8f30b851e
msgid "Secondly, they are disconnected from purpose. What the user needs to know might be things like:"
msgstr ""

#: d565a66adc174513806fc09530b51b1b
msgid "how much water to run, and how vigorously to run it, for a certain purpose"
msgstr ""

#: 45e25ff129c5457486d0d4be9904c2c9
msgid "what database configuration options align with particular real-world needs"
msgstr ""

#: 984aa54e479a4511bf1bf8d96f407089
msgid "How-to guides are about goals, projects and problems, not about tools."
msgstr ""

#: ae58651d067942dfaba46b230a2efc23
msgid "Tools appear in how-to guides as incidental bit-players, the means to the user's end. Sometimes of course, a particular end is closely aligned with a particular tool or part of the system, and then you will find that a how-to guide indeed concentrates on that. Just as often, a how-to guide will cut across different tools or parts of a system, joining them up together in a series of activities defined by something a human being needs to get done. In either case, it is that project that defines what a how-to guide must cover."
msgstr ""

#: 5fa1c852e4cd4f0fb5ddcb66ea5810ef
msgid "What how-to guides are not"
msgstr ""

#: bb129b8ac6704d6c89d1a1807cfc1691
msgid "**How-to guides are wholly distinct from tutorials**. They are often confused, but the user needs that they serve are quite different. Conflating them is at the root of many difficulties that afflict documentation. See :ref:`tutorials-how-to` for a discussion of this distinction."
msgstr ""

#: b0985b3ca7bf4bbf8e972cd6e3bb3f37
msgid "In another confusion, how-to guides are often construed merely as procedural guides. But solving a problem or accomplishing a task cannot always be reduced to a procedure. Real-world problems do not always offer themselves up to linear solutions. The sequences of action in a how-to guide sometimes need to fork and overlap, and they have multiple entry and exit-points. Often, a how-to guide will need the user to rely on their judgement in applying the guidance it can provide."
msgstr ""

#: 77a548f429f748b9b6ea35298ee5a6e1
msgid "Key principles"
msgstr ""

#: 2d1f48eac4a84613aa03f9f970523e4a
msgid "A how to-guide is concerned with work - a task or problem, with a practical goal. *Maintain focus on that goal*."
msgstr ""

#: 206f9166b8d3401c9930e2922ad15907
msgid "focused on tasks or problems"
msgstr ""

#: 8db575fc1af446a58ce7dbc44c58b496
msgid "assume the user knows what they want to achieve"
msgstr ""

#: 28383e2ba6cd48c0970d93833630dfc4
msgid "action and only action"
msgstr ""

#: 4c71c39039e74e78b35cacac0d884058
msgid "no digression, explanation, teaching"
msgstr ""

#: 1d284bd772004366b1ee00bd65265118
msgid "Anything else that's added distracts both you and the user and dilutes the useful power of the guide. Typically, the temptations are to explain or to provide reference for completeness. Neither of these are part of guiding the user in their work. They get in the way of the action; if they're important, link to them."
msgstr ""

#: 902970315a5f4354948c8f87e9caabbe
msgid "A how-to guide serves the work of the already-competent user, whom you can assume to know what they want to do, and to be able to follow your instructions correctly."
msgstr ""

#: 141da7131ccf4497a6089ff497c05954
msgid "Address real-world complexity"
msgstr ""

#: 0322269af1a844189cc6e6a0d645ac33
msgid "**A how-to guide needs to be adaptable to real-world use-cases**. One that is useless for any purpose except *exactly* the narrow one you have addressed is rarely valuable. You can't address every possible case, so you must find ways to remain open to the range of possibilities, in such a way that the user can adapt your guidance to their needs."
msgstr ""

#: 3faeb130c87848979b23d6f9cd5ace4b
msgid "Omit the unnecessary"
msgstr ""

#: 5e69fa076e874b6faee2b5f7d1372739
msgid "In how-to guides, **practical usability is more helpful than completeness.** Whereas a tutorial needs to be a complete, end-to-end guide, a how-to guide does not. It should start and end in some reasonable, meaningful place, and require the reader to join it up to their own work."
msgstr ""

#: d260c970a5164b90aac5f82b8dd3016d
msgid "Provide a set of instructions"
msgstr ""

#: 3c607cc8c3524376b5d46556920d96a1
msgid "A how-to guide describes an *executable solution* to a real-world problem or task. It's in the form of a contract: if you're facing this situation, then you can work your way through it by taking the steps outlined in this approach. The steps are in the form of *actions*."
msgstr ""

#: 6a5f4d8461894cdd8a87dbc5fdbb2e58
msgid "\"Actions\" in this context includes physical acts, but also thinking and judgement - solving a problem involves thinking it through. A how-to guide should address how the user thinks as well as what the user does."
msgstr ""

#: 391e680ef0d7415daab6dbb38b143a22
msgid "Describe a logical sequence"
msgstr ""

#: a8ded48e0e0b40ec8035cb1c4ab49da7
msgid "The fundamental structure of a how-to guide is a *sequence*. It implies logical ordering in time, that there is a sense and meaning to this particular order."
msgstr ""

#: 8dc2b8e9acbc45e491a9f6db4ae02858
msgid "In many cases, the ordering is simply imposed by the way things must be (step two requires completion of step one, for example). In this case it's obvious what order your directions should take."
msgstr ""

#: 6a5b95f252a74f3d9aa613057ab0b5d0
msgid "Sometimes the need is more subtle - it might be possible to *perform* two operations in either order, but if for example one operation helps set up the user's working environment or even their thinking in a way that benefits the other, that's a good reason for putting it first."
msgstr ""

#: bb32479cd4e34b689f3a3f8870e5154b
msgid "Seek flow"
msgstr ""

#: 565645698ae44dc0bf36ce10e08941be
msgid "At all times, try to ground your sequences in the patterns of the *user's* activities and thinking, in such a way that the guide acquires *flow*: smooth progress."
msgstr ""

#: d08e773906e741a1bf77c78bc58f0858
msgid "Achieving flow means successfully understanding the user. Paying attention to sense and meaning in ordering requires paying attention to the way human beings think and act, and the needs of someone following directions."
msgstr ""

#: c6f6757f14cd423a8c3f4b33571d94ec
msgid "Again, this can be somewhat obvious: a workflow that has the user repeatedly switching between contexts and tools is clearly clumsy and inefficient. But you should look more deeply than this. What are you asking the user to think about, and how will their thinking flow from subject to subject during their work? How long do you require the user to hold thoughts open before they can be resolved in action? If you require the user to jump back to earlier concerns, is this necessary or avoidable?"
msgstr ""

#: a45d63ffd4a84f749314832b58412c83
msgid "A how-to guide is concerned not just with logical ordering in time, but action taking place in time. Action, and a guide to it, has pace and rhythm. Badly-judged pace or disrupted rhythm are both damaging to flow."
msgstr ""

#: f9ace06d6cd44e109e8a87dd9026e3e3
msgid "At its best, how-to documentation gives the user flow. There is a distinct experience of encountering a guide that appears to *anticipate* the user - the documentation equivalent of a helper who has the tool you were about to reach for, ready to place it in your hand."
msgstr ""

#: 4148775d41844fbb98d35b66d45d9d73
msgid "Pay attention to naming"
msgstr ""

#: b840bb1e5e97404c98cc5bc21b3eaf12
msgid "**Choose titles that say exactly what a how-to guide shows.**"
msgstr ""

#: d4dae7b9c5ee4266a88bf87f5a713165
msgid "good: *How to integrate application performance monitoring*"
msgstr ""

#: 26715d701c864952995cfcbc8bcfc522
msgid "bad: *Integrating application performance monitoring* (maybe the document is about how to decide whether you should, not about how to do it)"
msgstr ""

#: 62cf6517c9c449fbbfcd6e25b0eaf179
msgid "very bad: *Application performance monitoring* (maybe it's about *how* - but maybe it's about *whether*, or even just an explanation of *what* it is)"
msgstr ""

#: 6294ff56582b4f1eb646f6ae015dd453
msgid "Note that search engines appreciate good titles just as much as humans do."
msgstr ""

#: 5fc3db9fb41d4e8eae9c8a917efa114d
msgid "The language of how-to guides"
msgstr ""

#: f40fc9879fda49ea85a36ba5a674d709
msgid "*This guide shows you how to...*"
msgstr ""

#: be94b43e0d554008b32359a106521af7
msgid "Describe clearly the problem or task that the guide shows the user how to solve."
msgstr ""

#: 84325dfc8c7a4915b0c861ff709d230a
msgid "*If you want x, do y. To achieve w, do z.*"
msgstr ""

#: 7ee259f0f2e94ebf986362daa62f15ee
msgid "Use conditional imperatives."
msgstr ""

#: 66ea8ce5b8f0438d8967d4550acbea73
msgid "*Refer to the x reference guide for a full list of options.*"
msgstr ""

#: 93c3567e1f8f441dbedeb0c8d8e513f2
msgid "Don't pollute your practical how-to guide with every possible thing the user might do related to x."
msgstr ""

#: 3ca854d21a90465e87f704a09a976507
msgid "Applied to food and cooking"
msgstr ""

#: 00f58dbc21f840c39ae8f25e72bec5cd
msgid "Consider a recipe, an excellent model for a how-to guide. A recipe clearly defines what will be achieved by following it, and **addresses a specific question** (*How do I make...?* or *What can I make with...?*)."
msgstr ""

#: 717dc319a93b4593804832f71d9b481d
msgid "A recipe contains a list of ingredients and a list of steps."
msgstr ""

#: 0fe834e37ff247399934f6d6bfd72919
msgid "It's not the responsibility of a recipe to *teach* you how to make something. A professional chef who has made exactly the same thing multiple times before may still follow a recipe - even if they *created* the recipe themselves - to ensure that they do it correctly."
msgstr ""

#: 27b9b2a9817949cd8140c1d5cec0bbcc
msgid "Even following a recipe **requires at least basic competence**. Someone who has never cooked before should not be expected to follow a recipe with success, so a recipe is not a substitute for a cooking lesson."
msgstr ""

#: cfe02a997774425c93cb08f211e47a42
msgid "Someone who expected to be provided with a recipe, and is given instead a cooking lesson, will be disappointed and annoyed. Similarly, while it's interesting to read about the context or history of a particular dish, the one time you don't want to be faced with that is while you are in the middle of trying to make it. A good recipe follows a well-established format, that excludes both teaching and discussion, and focuses only on **how** to make the dish concerned."
msgstr ""
